{"id":"000W8T","title":"ɹɹ∀, with Calvinball (Arrows and Ambiguous Modifiers)","author":"Oddlyeven","solvedCount":3,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-27T02:56:05+00:00","posted":"Heute, 01:03 Uhr","rules":"This is a collaboration between Calvinball and myself for a Skunkworks event where you had to make a puzzle with an anonymous partner and only found out who they were after the puzzles had been submitted. We hope you enjoy!\n\nRules: Normal Sudoku rules apply. Put the digits 1 to 9 once each into every row, column and 3x3 box.\n\nHalvers/Negators: One cell in every row, column and box is a modifier cell. Every digit from 1 to 9 appears exactly once in the set of modifier cells. Each modifer cell is either a halver or a negator. A halver cell's value is half the digit (e.g. 9 becomes 4.5). A negator cell's value is minus the digit (e.g. 9 becomes negative 9). The value of an unmodifed cell is equal to its digit.\n\nArrows: The value in an arrow's circle is equal to the sum of the values on the attached arrow. Values are allowed to repeat on an arrow as normally allowed by other rules.\n\nLinks:\n\nSudokuPad: https://sudokupad.app/7r9bvzityv","solutionCode":"Column 9, top to bottom (9 digits).","tags":["Sudoku","Arrows (Variante)","Modifier Cells (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/7r9bvzityv","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/7r9bvzityv","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":10,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-27T02:56:05+00:00"}